<title>FRANCE: Iraq passed on U.S. wheat import tender - traders.</title>
<headline>Iraq passed on U.S. wheat import tender - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq has passed on offers in a tender for the purchase of 50,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat, European grain exporters said.</p>
<p>The tender, launched a few weeks ago, came under a United Nations-monitored oil-for-food deal, with delivery slated for June.</p>
<p>Traders did not know if or when Iraq planned to retender for U.S. wheat, although some exporters said this was unlikely.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
